From: Trijal Saha <97483939+Trijal08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ims-config: split the hidden menu the way stock does

Stock does not send its IMS configuration as one message. Every stack in
all five 2026-11-06 captures gets three, and the split is identical each
time:

    1492B   identity and SIP timers, then the whole carrier block, then
            the video capability descriptor (tag 771)
      14B   the identity extras -- 777, 782, 783, and 778 for a card with
            an ISIM, which makes it 51B
     448B   the carrier block on its own, the same 63 records again

`ImsConfig::group()` returns those three sets, and the FFI exposes them as
`samsung_ims_config_group()`. The full entry list is unchanged, so a caller
that wants one message still gets exactly what it got before.

This is not tidiness. Measured with the rings instrument at 20 Hz across a
real stall, the CP does not emit its registration indication while the link
is idle -- `fmt rx undrained` was 0 in all 115 samples of the window, so
nothing was queued and no notification had been lost -- and the AP's next
write is what frees it. Stock's grant-to-registration is 0.7-2.5 s on all
ten stack-boots because its three pushes keep writing; our single push left
the stack silent for twelve seconds and registration waited for whatever
polled next.

Tag 778 also moves ahead of the empty pair so the identity push reads
777, 778, 782, 783 as stock's does.
